  "summary_en": "Swiss Federal Assembly amendment to the Road Traffic Act adopted 17 March 2023. It creates a legal basis for vehicles with automation systems, driverless vehicles on approved routes under operator supervision, mandatory tamper-protected driving-mode data recorders, data access rules, and ASTRA-approved trials, alongside unrelated penalty changes.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines vehicles with an automation system and lets the Federal Council relieve drivers of duties.",
   "Driverless vehicles allowed only on cantonally defined routes and supervised by an operator.",
   "Mandatory non-deactivatable, tamper-protected driving-mode recorder logging activation, takeover requests, emergencies and faults.",
   "Data access rules for keepers, authorities, with deletion deadlines and anonymised transfer to ASTRA.",
   "ASTRA may approve time-limited trials with derogations and fund pilot projects up to 50%."
  ],
